{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhNeGH1vd2azsz7hWgX4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed: `paginate` now returns every item on each page, including the last item of a full page and a final partial page.\n\n**Cause:** the end index in `src/pagination.ts:5` was computed as `start + pageSize - 1`, but `slice` already excludes its end index, so each full page came back one item short.\n\n**Change:** one line, dropping the `- 1`:\n\n```ts\nconst end = Math.min(start + pageSize, items.length);\n```\n\nThe signature and validation are untouched.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `npm test` passes 4/4, but those tests only cover the empty collection, an out-of-range page, and invalid arguments, so none of them exercised this bug.\n- I also ran a one-off spot check on 7 items with page size 3: pages 1–4 return `[1,2,3]`, `[4,5,6]`, `[7]`, `[]`, and a page size of 7 or 10 returns all seven items.\n\nI did not add a regression test, since you asked that tests not be modified; a page-boundary case in `test/pagination.test.ts` would be worth adding."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":339,"cache_read_input_tokens":8678,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":339},"output_tokens":347,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"58de6639-7ca5-4dd7-bbb7-01b0331f1918","uuid":"c3c94264-3e19-4d26-9fbd-842d39667631","timestamp":"2026-10-04T14:43:04.044Z","request_id":"req_011CfhNeG1dwWcMiKRZCUNRt"}
